  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 General Election (November 3, 2026) - Elections - Delaware County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n Delaware County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Delaware County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 General Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \n2009 \n2008 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 General Election\n\n \nNovember 3, 2026\n General Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n\n \n \nImportant Dates \n \n \n \nTuesday, August 25, 2026 - First day to submit Absentee Ballot requests \n \nWednesday, October 14, 2026 - First Day to Mail Absentee Ballots to Voters and First Day to Vote In-Person at the County Auditor's Office \n \nMonday, October 19, 2026 - Voter Pre-Registration Deadline, Last Day to Request an Absentee Ballot by Mail, County Auditor's Office Open from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. \n \nMonday, November 2, 2026 - 4:30 p.m. - In-Person Absentee Voting Ends \n \nTuesday, November 3, 2026 - General Election Day \n \n \n\nPre-registered voters are now required to provide an approved form of identification at the polling place before receiving and casting a regular ballot. Voters who are not pre-registered (such as voters registering on Election Day, and voters changing precincts), must also provide proof of residence.  The following documents can be used as proof of residency if they contain your name and current address, and are current within 45 days:  Residential lease, utility bill, bank statement, paycheck, government check or other government document, or a property tax statement (current within 45 days of final payment date).  Voters who are unable to provide an approved form of identification (or prove residence if required), may have their identities attested to by another registered voter in the precinct, or have the right to cast a provisional ballot.  Attesters must also provide an approved form of identification.  For additional information about providing proof of identity and/or residency, you may visit the Secretary of State’s website at: https://sos.iowa.gov/voterid, or contact the Delaware County Auditor’s Office at 563-927-4701.  \n \n\nPre-Election Day voter registration for this election will close Monday, October  19, 2026, at 5:00 p.m.  It is highly recommended that those persons wishing to vote in this election should pre-register on or before the October 19, 2026 deadline.  Eligible persons have the right to register to vote and cast a ballot on Election Day if they are able to provide proof of both their identity and residency at the polls.  Please bring a valid and current photo ID that has an expiration date.  If the address on your ID is not current, you will also need to provide proof of residency.  \n \n\nAbsentee Voting \n \n\nAbsentee voting begins Wednesday, October 14, 2026. To request an absentee ballot, you may either pick up a request form or complete this form and submit it to the Delaware County Auditor's Office (301 E. Main Street, Manchester, IA 52057). Make sure you fill out the form completely, sign and date the form and mail it to the Delaware County Auditor. The last day to request an absentee ballot to be mailed to your home is Monday, October 19, 2026, at 5:00 p.m.    \n \n\nIn-person absentee voting is available at the Delaware County Auditor's Office during regular business hours (8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.) beginning Wednesday, October 14, 2026, until Monday, November 2, 2026.  We will also be open two Saturdays: October 24, 2026 from 8:00a.m. to 12:00p.m. and October 31, 2026 from 9:00a.m. to 5:00p.m.  \n \n\nCurbside voting is also available.  If you have any questions regarding the absentee process, please contact the Delaware County Auditor’s Office by phone at 563-927-4701 or by e-mail at auditor@co.delaware.ia.us. \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Results Available on Election Night\n \n \n\n 0 Precincts Counted\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n\n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n Adams / Hazel Green \n \n \n\n Adams / Hazel Green (Kirkwood)\n \n \n\n Colony\n \n \n\n Delhi / Delaware Corp (Lake)\n \n \n\n Delhi / Delaware Corp\n \n \n\n Honey Creek / Elk\n \n \n\n Manchester Ward 1\n \n \n\n Manchester Ward 2\n \n \n\n Manchester Ward 3\n \n \n\n Milo / Prairie (Lake)\n \n \n\n Milo / Prairie\n \n \n\n Oneida / North Fork / Bremen\n \n \n\n Richland / Coffins Grove\n \n \n\n South Fork / Union (Kirkwood)\n \n \n\n South Fork / Union\n \n \n\n Full Constitutional Amendment\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Delaware County, Iowa, Elections website at https://delawarecountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Delaware County Courthouse\n\n 301 E Main St, Manchester, IA 52057\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Delaware County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday \n \n8:00 AM - 4:30 PM \n \nContact Numbers\n\n Phone: (563) 927-4701\n \nFax: (563) 927-6423 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
